    <data xml:space="preserve" name="HelpText">
        <value>Space: Play/Pause outside controls that own Space
Ctrl+O / Ctrl+Shift+O: Add files / folder
Ctrl+F: Search; Esc: Clear search
Enter / Delete / Ctrl+A: Play / remove / select visible rows (playlist focus)
Alt+Left / Alt+Right: Previous / Next
Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right: Seek 5 seconds
Ctrl+Up / Ctrl+Down: App volume 5 percentage points
Ctrl+N: New playlist; F2: Rename (tab focus)
Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down: Reorder rows after clearing search
F1: Local help

Command line: local file/folder paths append without autoplay; --play explicitly starts the first added item. -- ends option parsing. A second launch activates the existing per-user instance. No arguments never start audio.

Tray: Show/Hide, Play/Pause, Next, Previous, Exit. Closing exits by default; close-to-tray is an explicit preference. Language changes apply immediately after Apply.

Sources remain unchanged. Ratings, history, library, queue and settings are stored locally. Restore never starts audio. Only local, available offline files are accepted. No application network requests. BASS and add-on distribution terms remain a release gate; this is a development build.

Backup creates a complete local ZIP of database and settings. Restore backup validates it, retains current files and never autoplays. Music/cache/logs are excluded; legacy .db restore changes only the database. Restart for a restored language change.

Settings include accent, waveform style, startup/session options and local cache usage/clear. Playlist duplicate removal previews exact file/CUE matches and keeps the first occurrence. Local diagnostics are previewed and personal paths hidden before copying.</value>
